\title{tsintermittent: Intermittent Time Series Forecasting}
\description{
Time series methods for intermittent demand forecasting. The package
includes Croston's method and its variants (SBA and SBJ), Croston-style moving
averages, the TSB method, and simple exponential smoothing, with parameters and
initial values that can be optimised using cost functions designed for intermittent
demand (Kourentzes, 2014). Intermittent time series classification and iMAPA, which
combines forecasts from multiple temporal aggregation levels, are also provided
(Petropoulos and Kourentzes, 2015). Empirical predictive distributions of the demand
over the lead time can be calculated for all methods.
}
\section{Forecasting methods}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link{crost}}: Croston's method, SBA, and SBJ.
\item \code{\link{crost.ma}}: Croston-style moving averages.
\item \code{\link{tsb}}: TSB method.
\item \code{\link{sexsm}}: Simple exponential smoothing.
\item \code{\link{imapa}}: iMAPA, combining forecasts from multiple temporal
aggregation levels.
\item \code{\link{data.frc}}: Forecasting multiple series with a single call.
}
}

